{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '11335,11435p' && rg -n '7\\\\.3|D742|third blind run|instrument' AGENTS.md docs/CURRENT_STATE.md docs/DECISIONS.md\"","aggregated_output":" 11335\t    on total capex used as data-center capex (R09).\n 11336\t- **Council round 55** (`codex-r55.md`):\n 11337\t  - STOP is correct as registered, and the counts reconcile (three wordings corrected).\n 11338\t  - R06 and R12 are the same method, so the readers' boundary is unstable.\n 11339\t  - The three rulings go to Alex.\n 11340\t  - **Next:**\n 11341\t    - fix the S1 range;\n 11342\t    - apply the rulings, in the reader brief and in code only where the structure decides them;\n 11343\t    - verify both reader families on the stored boundary replies;\n 11344\t    - re-run the registered blind test once with fresh writers and readers, then the paid re-send request.\n 11345\t\n 11346\t## D741 · 2026-11-22 · Alex rules the three reader questions of D740\n 11347\t\n 11348\t- **The questions** (after D740), each with its options; the recommended option is listed first:\n 11349\t  - 【增速参考】\"写手用公司指引的三季度 1080 亿算出“指引隐含增速约 12%”，参考它定四季度增速 13%，再套在自己预测的三季度 1136 亿上。进入收入计算的三季度数只有 1136 亿这一个。这算不算“同一季度用了两个数”的错？\" Options: 不算错 (推荐); 算错.\n 11350\t  - 【市场参照】\"分析师预期公司全年总收入 4110 亿，最近一个季度数据中心占 92.5%，乘出来约 3800 亿。能不能把这 3800 亿叫作“市场对数据中心全年的预期”？\" Options: 不能 (推荐); 能.\n 11351\t  - 【总开支当数据中心开支】\"问题问四大云厂商“数据中心资本开支”，原文只给了“总资本开支”（并说大部分投向 AI 基础设施）。一份答案直接拿总开支当数据中心开支，没扣非数据中心的部分。可以吗？\" Options: 必须写明扣多少 (推荐); 可以直接用.\n 11352\t- **Alex's answers** (2026-11-22): \"不算错 (推荐)\"; \"不能 (推荐)\"; \"必须写明扣多少 (推荐)\".\n 11353\t- **Decided (Alex):**\n 11354\t  1. **Not a defect:** a growth rate computed from guidance and used only as a stated benchmark for an estimate, when one figure\n 11355\t     supplies the quarter in the revenue calculation.\n 11356\t  2. **Not the market's reference:** consensus for a total × a past quarter's reported share. That figure is our comparison estimate.\n 11357\t     Only an outside figure for the member's own quantity (for example Morningstar's direct segment estimate), or a calculation that\n 11358\t     carries no past period's reported share or multiple to another period, is the market's reference.\n 11359\t  3. **A total used for a narrower quantity** (total capex for data-center capex) must state the deduction as its own figure, or give\n 11360\t     a supported bound that shows where the narrower quantity lands.\n 11361\t- **How they are applied (D738):**\n 11362\t  - Ruling 2's carried share is structural, so S5 refuses it.\n 11363\t  - Rulings 1 and 3 go in the request and in the reader brief, because they turn on what a label or an estimate means.\n 11364\t  - Then three steps:\n 11365\t    1. fix the S1 \"from … to …\" range (D740);\n 11366\t    2. check that both reader families apply the rulings the same way to the stored boundary replies;\n 11367\t    3. re-run the registered blind test once with fresh writers and readers.\n 11368\t\n 11369\t## D742 · 2026-11-22 · The v13s re-run stops on one sound answer refused by S4; council 56–56c keeps S4 and makes the request state one benchmark rule; a third $0 blind run follows\n 11370\t\n 11371\t- **The result** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND2-RESULT.md`, run `poc/data/judging-v13s-blind2-2026-11-22/`):\n 11372\t  - **STOP on one confirmed registered line.** S4 refused P-v4's Claude writer, whose Q4 = apply_growth(own Q3 $112.5B, growth(Q2\n 11373\t    $96.2B, Q3 guidance $108B)).\n 11374\t    - Both refusal reviewers marked the condition stated and the answer right.\n 11375\t    - Both readers and both adjudicators called the forecast supported.\n 11376\t  - **Every other line passes:**\n 11377\t    - 12 of 12 schema-valid, 11 of 12 accepted;\n 11378\t    - every case usable;\n 11379\t    - the joint case supported in one reply;\n 11380\t    - no settled defect: 5 marks jointly rejected, 9 split, 0 jointly upheld.\n 11381\t  - **Two reader splits, disclosed, not stops:**\n 11382\t    - O's \"$18 billion committed … for the remainder of its fiscal year\" read as part of the $25B balance paid by year-end. It decides\n 11383\t      O's rung, and D741 ruling 2 does not settle it.\n 11384\t    - Wrong numbers in prose that no figure carries (R03, R09, R11). The registered defect types cover figures only.\n 11385\t- **The mechanism.** The request pulled three ways, and the writer followed the system text:\n 11386\t  - the system text: \"a run-rate that carries the guided growth forward\";\n 11387\t  - the schema: a benchmark \"for an estimate\";\n 11388\t  - the header: every path through the forecast.\n 11389\t  S4 matches Alex's ruling 1 as written (\"used only as a stated benchmark for an estimate\").\n 11390\t- **The council rounds:**\n 11391\t  - Round 56 (`codex-r56.md`) confirmed the STOP. It rejected Claude's blanket stop at any % or x figure: a reply building Q4 on the\n 11392\t    guided $108B through a multiple applied twice to Q2 would publish beside Q3 = $112.5B.\n 11393\t  - Round 56b (`codex-r56b.md`) rejected a narrowed `apply_growth` exemption. Arithmetic can pull the forecast back to guidance inside\n 11394\t    the base, and equivalent forms landed on opposite sides of the line.\n 11395\t  - Round 56c (`codex-r56c.md`) chose to keep S4, to state one rule in the request, and to register the refusal review's two judgements\n 11396\t    up front.\n 11397\t- **Decided (council, under Alex's \"那你自己持续迭代\" and D741 ruling 1):**\n 11398\t  1. **S4 is unchanged.**\n 11399\t  2. **The request states one rule** in the system text, the schema and the header:\n 11400\t     - guidance informs the pace;\n 11401\t     - the forecast pace is recorded as an estimate naming its benchmark in `rests_on`;\n 11402\t     - the quarter's dollar value is the one forecast figure;\n 11403\t     - the header says the first figure of a shared quantity reached on every arithmetic path, through rates and multiples too, is its\n 11404\t       forecast.\n 11405\t  3. **The readers' brief and the adjudication header** keep Alex's sentence and add: look through any rate or multiple, including\n 11406\t     inside a stated assumption, for a second dollar value. The adjudication packet now includes the system text.\n 11407\t  4. **The refusal review** records \"sound\" and \"stated\" apart. A sound answer refused under a clearly stated condition still stops.\n 11408\t     The stop lines are unchanged (`SMALL-DESIGN.md` §5 [D742]).\n 11409\t  5. **Part A:** cases 109 of 109 (5 new); mutants 42 of 42 (1 new); rehearsal 19 of 19. The v13 plan hash is unchanged (6f81dae5…),\n 11410\t     and the v13s plan changes as intended.\n 11411\t  6. **`s4_replay.py` on the saved reply.** The reply as written and both council resets are refused. The stated-estimate form passes\n 11412\t     at $416.62B.\n 11413\t  7. **One fresh $0 blind run follows** (12 writers), because the request bytes changed. A fresh sound refusal, or an accepted reply\n 11414\t     confirmed to carry two values of a quarter, goes back to council. Only a run meeting every line goes to Alex for the paid re-send.\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:448:**The one next task: run the third v13s blind test (12 fresh writers, then readers, reviewers and adjudicators) on the request D742\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:449:fixed, and score it on the registered lines (`research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md` §5 [D742]).**\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:451:- **The re-run stopped on one line** (D742, `research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND2-RESULT.md`).\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:469:The record before D742:\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:471:**Earlier next task (done, D742): re-run the v13s blind test once with fresh writers and readers, after the reader calibration on\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:658:  - every reading instrument built and passed by the council before any output was read: reading tools in round 5, the §1.6 tools in\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:338:one draw (D238; §7.3); the extraction standard page is the step's PRD and AGENTS §6–§7 carry the principles (D242; §6, §7).\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:735:| D391 | 2026-11-09 | Close clean Step 1 on c8 (focused D388 call not adopted); every change states its expected effect on a reader or the final judgement first (AGENTS §7.3) | in force | AGENTS §7.3; round log §59 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:744:| D400 | 2026-11-10 | Stage A of the clean ladder step is read against Alex's absolute lines with no paid control arm (an exception to AGENTS §7.3 for this first measurement); the lines are fixed; every report says it does not compare with production | in force | `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md` §8 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:756:| D412 | 2026-11-10 | Every round is reflected on in the council to a recorded consensus, then the next test goes straight ahead, held to the PRD and its quantified goals; every trace is read by Claude itself | in force | AGENTS §7.3; round log §69 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:1018:| D674 | 2026-11-17 | Alex's goal: run and keep tackling until the comparison's criteria pass; council loop on the traces after each round that does not pass; no questions to Alex; no scope drift; frozen ruler and instruments never moved; every try logged in TRIES.md | in force | D674 record |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:1086:| D742 | 2026-11-22 | v13s re-run STOP: S4 refused a sound answer that computed a guidance rate straight into Q4 (request pulled three ways); council 56–56c: blanket and narrowed exemptions both let a reset to guidance publish, so S4 stays and the request states one rule (guidance informs the pace; the pace is an estimate naming its benchmark; the quarter's dollar value is the one forecast); refusal review registers sound and stated apart; two reader splits disclosed (O's $18B reading, prose numbers); third $0 blind run next | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND2-RESULT.md` |\nAGENTS.md:39:  work, as one recommendation and one test (§7.3). Settle wording, placement and where a rule is written yourself, and say so in the\nAGENTS.md:326:### 7.3 Iterating\nAGENTS.md:428:  allows (§7.3) starts only on his explicit word (Alex, 2026-10-27: \"我不是要你看下step 1抽取到底行不行？\").\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && nl -ba BLIND3-RESULT.md && rg -n '§5|\"'^## |'\"\\\\[D742\\\\]' SMALL-DESIGN.md && rg -n 'READER_BRIEF|adjudicat|named def' blind_test.py && rg -n 'def v13s_schema|band it overlaps|S6|def .*rung' render_v13.py calc_small.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && nl -ba BLIND3-RESULT.md && rg -n '§5|\"'^## |'\"\\\\[D742\\\\]' SMALL-DESIGN.md && rg -n 'READER_BRIEF|adjudicat|named def' blind_test.py && rg -n 'def v13s_schema|band it overlaps|S6|def .*rung' render_v13.py calc_small.py\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# judging-v13s blind test, third run after D742: result (SMALL-DESIGN.md §5 [D742])\n     2\t\n     3\t**STOP on one registered line, as written:** \"an accepted reply with a named defect (marked by both readers …)\".\n     4\t- **R01 (S, Claude writer).** Both readers marked \"broken structure\" on F14: the outcome is a range of $679.25–745B, and rung 4\n     5\t  ($700–800B) does not hold all of it.\n     6\t- **Both adjudicators reject that mark.** The schema the writer was given says the rung is \"for a range outcome, a band it overlaps,\n     7\t  with the reason in reasons\". The answer gives that reason: \"the midpoint and most of the range lie in rung 4\". The code (S6) checks\n     8\t  overlap.\n     9\t- **The cause is my reader brief.** Its definition of broken structure reads \"a rung whose band does not hold the outcome\", without the\n    10\t  schema's range clause. Both readers applied the brief as written. No earlier run had a range that crossed a rung edge, so the gap was\n    11\t  not exercised before.\n    12\t\n    13\tEverything else in the run is clean:\n    14\t- **Writers:** 12 of 12 schema-valid, 12 of 12 accepted, 0 refusals, so there was no refusal review.\n    15\t- **Readers and adjudicators:** six packets drew a disagreement. Every disputed mark was settled, and every one was rejected by both\n    16\t  adjudicators. No defect was upheld, and no split remains.\n    17\t- **Every case has a usable reply.** The joint case has both forecasts supported in one reply (R02 and R11).\n    18\t- **The D742 rule was followed by every P-family writer.** All six recorded the Q4 pace as an estimate naming its benchmark, then\n    19\t  computed Q4 from it. None computed a guidance rate straight into the calculation.\n    20\t\n    21\t**Run:** `poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/`, $0 at the provider. All Codex writers read only `system.txt`, `user.txt` and\n    22\t`schema.json`. The tally is in `TALLY.json`.\n    23\t\n    24\t## 1. Writers' first answers (`CHECKED.json`)\n    25\t\n    26\t| Case | Claude writer | Codex writer |\n    27\t|---|---|---|\n    28\t| P (joint) | v4 416.3, v8 386.1, both rung 2 | v4 420.9, v8 391.0, both rung 2 |\n    29\t| P-v4 | 419.3, rung 2 | 416.3, rung 2 |\n    30\t| P-v8 | 387.4, rung 2 | 388.1, rung 2 |\n    31\t| S (CY2026) | 679.25–745, rung 4 | 670.5, rung 3 |\n    32\t| O | 9–20, rung 1 | 16, rung 1 |\n    33\t| E | 37, rung 3 | 34, rung 3 |\n    34\t\n    35\t## 2. Readers and adjudicators (`TALLY.json`)\n    36\t\n    37\t**Settled as not defects (both adjudicators reject):**\n    38\t- R01 broken structure (both readers' marks), explained above;\n    39\t- R01 \"two forecasts\" (Microsoft backed out of the four-company tallies, a reader matter through `rests_on`);\n    40\t- three \"plus or minus 2%\" midpoints (R02, R09) and a rounding difference within tolerance (R08);\n    41\t- R06's \"number misread\" claims on the $18B schedule and the Lancium tranche.\n    42\t\n    43\t**Support:**\n    44\t- **R07 (S, Codex writer) is settled \"not supported\".** Its rung rests on a 90% data-center share, while the passages put the share near\n    45\t  100%:\n    46\t  - e1947: more than $730B \"on AI infrastructure\" against $720–745B of capex;\n    47\t  - e2759 and e5376: NVIDIA's \"nearly $800 billion\" for the top five, written both as capex and as data-center capex;\n    48\t  - Meta's own figures: about 96%.\n    49\t  At 94% or more, the same $745B gives rung 4. The reply is accepted and publishable, but its rung does not follow from the evidence.\n    50\t  This is not a registered stop line (usable is counted per case, and S has R01). It is a real judgement error in an answer that would\n    51\t  publish.\n    52\t- **R06 (O, Claude writer) is split again** on the $18B reading: Codex says not supported, Claude says supported. This is the same\n    53\t  passage as in both earlier runs.\n    54\t- Every other forecast is supported by both readers or both adjudicators.\n    55\t\n    56\t## 3. What the test shows\n    57\t\n    58\t- **The writer-side contract holds.** In three runs, the request has moved from 11 of 12 accepted with a checker error (run 1), to 11 of\n    59\t  12 with a request contradiction (run 2), to 12 of 12 with no refusal (run 3). D742's rule was followed by all six writers it applies\n    60\t  to.\n    61\t- **The stop this time is in the measuring instrument.** The reader brief's definition is narrower than the format the writer was\n    62\t  given. Both adjudicators corrected it from the format rule.\n    63\t- **The readers did their job on substance.** They found the one reply whose decisive assumption is unsupported (R07). That is the\n    64\t  kind of error the paid re-send is meant to measure in gpt-6-luna.\n    65\t- **Open disclosures:**\n    66\t  - O's $18B reading (split three runs running);\n    67\t  - wrong numbers in prose, which this run's adjudications did not raise;\n    68\t  - R07's unsupported share.\n19:## 1. What is dropped, and where it goes\n32:## 2. The rules code enforces (revised after round 52, `codex-r52.md`; the revision is marked [52])\n59:## 2-old. The rules as first written (superseded by the revision above)\n78:## 3. The wire schema, word for word (examples from no covered company, AGENTS §6)\n143:## 4. Build\n162:## 5. The $0 blind test (registered; REPAIR-DESIGN.md §5 with rounds 51's fixes)\n279:**[D742] Registered before the third run (council rounds 56–56c).** The re-run stopped on one S4 refusal of a sound answer\n157:READER_BRIEF = \"\"\"# Blind reading (judging-v13s blind test, SMALL-DESIGN.md §5)\n208:        (folder / f'{pid}.md').write_text(READER_BRIEF + '\\n# The request as the writer saw it\\n\\n' + it['user'] + '\\n\\n# The answer\\n\\n' + raw + '\\n')\nrender_v13.py:81:def v13s_schema(member_ids, evidence_ids, theme_ids):\nrender_v13.py:145:                          '(a band includes its lower edge, not its upper); for a range outcome, a band it overlaps, with the reason in reasons.'}),\ncalc_small.py:3:quarter, S5 an own estimate passed off as the market's) and for broken structure (S6, S7), and only where the calculation's own\ncalc_small.py:162:    `reference`; marker errors go in `decode_errors` (S5, S6, S7). An empty string counts as absent.\"\"\"\ncalc_small.py:193:                errors.append(('S6', f'{v}: {len(outs)} figures are marked as its outcome; exactly one is required'))\ncalc_small.py:562:            errors.append(('S6', f'{v}: its outcome {out[\"id\"]} must be your own forecast (a computed or estimate figure with basis forecast)'))\ncalc_small.py:564:            errors.append(('S6', f'{v}: outcome {out[\"id\"]} measures {\" | \".join(_key(out[\"what\"]))}, not the question\\'s {\" | \".join(_key(member[\"what\"]))}'))\ncalc_small.py:566:            errors.append(('S6', f'{v}: outcome {out[\"id\"]} is in {out[\"unit\"]}, not {member.get(\"unit\", \"USD bn\")}'))\ncalc_small.py:570:            errors.append(('S6', f'{v}: rung {rung!r} is not one of 1..{len(member[\"bands\"])}'))\ncalc_small.py:575:            errors.append(('S6', f'{v}: rung {rung} {member[\"bands\"][rung - 1]} does not hold its outcome {shown} as recomputed'))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
