{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && nl -ba blind_test.py | sed -n '1,280p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t\"\"\"The v13s blind conformance test (SMALL-DESIGN.md §5 with its [52] changes; D737, D738). $0 at the provider.\n     2\t\n     3\t  python3 blind_test.py build <out folder>      # the six registered requests, each in its own folder (system.txt, user.txt, schema.json)\n     4\t  python3 blind_test.py check <out folder>      # every writer's first answer through model.check_schema, from_answer and check\n     5\t  python3 blind_test.py packets <out folder>    # one reader packet per answer: the whole request text and the answer, checker hidden\n     6\t\n     7\tWriters put their first answer, unedited, at <out>/<case>/answers/<writer>.json (the writer label never reaches a reader).\n     8\t\"\"\"\n     9\timport hashlib\n    10\timport json\n    11\timport random\n    12\timport re\n    13\timport sqlite3\n    14\timport sys\n    15\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    16\t\n    17\tHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n    18\tREPO = HERE.parents[2]\n    19\tsys.path.insert(0, str(HERE))\n    20\tsys.path.insert(0, str(REPO / 'src'))\n    21\timport calc_small as cs  # noqa: E402\n    22\timport paid_gate as pg  # noqa: E402\n    23\tfrom hivemind import model  # noqa: E402\n    24\t\n    25\tW = pg.W\n    26\tCASES = {   # registered in SMALL-DESIGN.md §5: archive, calls, member keys\n    27\t    'P': {'draw': 'old-1', 'calls': [('v4', 8810), ('v8', 8816)], 'arm': 'joint'},\n    28\t    'P-v4': {'draw': 'old-1', 'calls': [('v4', 8810), ('v8', 8816)], 'arm': 'separate', 'member': 'v4'},\n    29\t    'P-v8': {'draw': 'old-1', 'calls': [('v4', 8810), ('v8', 8816)], 'arm': 'separate', 'member': 'v8'},\n    30\t    'S': {'draw': 'old-3', 'calls': [('v6', 9043)], 'arm': 'single',\n    31\t          'what': W('four largest AI hyperscalers', 'data-center capex', 'combined', 'CY2026')},\n    32\t    'O': {'draw': 'old-2', 'calls': [('v29', 8507)], 'arm': 'single', 'what': W('NVIDIA', 'equity investment commitments', 'company', 'end of FY2027'),\n    33\t          'note': pg.O_NOTE},\n    34\t    'E': {'draw': 'old-3', 'calls': [('v41', 9071)], 'arm': 'single', 'what': W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', 'Vera CPU', 'FY2028')},\n    35\t}\n    36\tREGISTERED_QUESTIONS = {\n    37\t    ('old-1', 'v4'): \"What will NVIDIA's total revenue be in FY2027?\",\n    38\t    ('old-1', 'v8'): 'How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?',\n    39\t    ('old-3', 'v6'): 'How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026?',\n    40\t    ('old-2', 'v29'): \"How much will NVIDIA's equity investment commitments reach at the publication of its FY2027 annual report?\",\n    41\t    ('old-3', 'v41'): 'What will NVIDIA report as Vera CPU revenue for FY2028?',\n    42\t}\n    43\tREGISTERED_EDGES = {('old-1', 'v4'): [431.2, 392.0, 352.8, 313.6], ('old-1', 'v8'): [400.0, 350.0, 300.0, 250.0],\n    44\t                    ('old-3', 'v6'): [500.0, 600.0, 700.0, 800.0], ('old-2', 'v29'): [25.0, 50.0, 75.0, 100.0],\n    45\t                    ('old-3', 'v41'): [50.0, 40.0, 30.0, 20.0]}\n    46\t\n    47\t\n    48\tdef heading(draw, call_id):\n    49\t    a = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{pg.RUN / draw / \"prod/archive.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    50\t    user = json.loads(a.execute('select request_json from model_calls where call_id=?', (call_id,)).fetchone()[0])['messages'][1]['content']\n    51\t    m = re.match(r'Thesis (v\\d+) \\([^)]*\\): ([^\\n]*)', user)\n    52\t    return m.group(1), m.group(2)\n    53\t\n    54\t\n    55\tdef edges(bands):\n    56\t    out = []\n    57\t    for lo, hi in bands:\n    58\t        for e in (lo, hi):\n    59\t            if e is not None and e not in out:\n    60\t                out.append(e)\n    61\t    return out\n    62\t\n    63\t\n    64\tdef build_case(name, spec):\n    65\t    draw = spec['draw']\n    66\t    for view_id, call_id in spec['calls']:                     # the registered heading, question and ladder, or refuse\n    67\t        tid, question = heading(draw, call_id)\n    68\t        if tid != view_id or question != REGISTERED_QUESTIONS[(draw, view_id)]:\n    69\t            raise SystemExit(f'{name}: call {call_id} heads {tid} \"{question}\", not the registered {view_id}')\n    70\t        got = edges(pg.bands(draw, view_id))\n    71\t        if got != REGISTERED_EDGES[(draw, view_id)]:                   # [54] in rung order, not sorted\n    72\t            raise SystemExit(f'{name}: {view_id} ladder edges {got}, not the registered {REGISTERED_EDGES[(draw, view_id)]}')\n    73\t    if spec['arm'] in ('joint', 'separate'):\n    74\t        (tv, tc), (dv, dc) = spec['calls']\n    75\t        family = pg.small_family(pg.pair_family(draw, (tv, tc), (dv, dc)), pg.PAIR_SCOPES)\n    76\t        if spec['arm'] == 'joint':\n    77\t            return pg.item(f'blind-{name}', 'joint', draw, spec['calls'], family, [tv, dv], 'v13s')\n    78\t        return pg.item(f'blind-{name}', f'separate-{spec[\"member\"]}', draw, spec['calls'], pg.only(family, spec['member']), [spec['member']], 'v13s')\n    79\t    view_id, call_id = spec['calls'][0]\n    80\t    family = {'members': {view_id: {'what': spec['what'], 'bands': pg.bands(draw, view_id)}}, 'relations': [], 'shared': [], 'compare_periods': []}\n    81\t    family = pg.small_family(family, notes={view_id: spec['note']} if spec.get('note') else None)\n    82\t    return pg.item(f'blind-{name}', 'single', draw, spec['calls'], family, [view_id], 'v13s')\n    83\t\n    84\t\n    85\tdef build(out):\n    86\t    if out.exists():\n    87\t        raise SystemExit(f'{out} exists')\n    88\t    gate_quotes = {p['text'] for it in json.loads((HERE / 'paid-plan.json').read_text()) for p in it['passages'].values()}\n    89\t    report = []\n    90\t    for name, spec in CASES.items():\n    91\t        it = build_case(name, spec)\n    92\t        folder = out / name\n    93\t        (folder / 'answers').mkdir(parents=True)\n    94\t        (folder / 'system.txt').write_text(it['system'])\n    95\t        (folder / 'user.txt').write_text(it['user'])\n    96\t        (folder / 'schema.json').write_text(json.dumps(it['schema'], indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))\n    97\t        (folder / 'item.json').write_text(json.dumps(it, ensure_ascii=False))\n    98\t        fresh = sum(1 for p in it['passages'].values() if p['text'] not in gate_quotes)\n    99\t        report.append(f'{name:5} {it[\"arm\"]:13} members {it[\"members\"]} passages {len(it[\"passages\"])} ({fresh} quotes absent from the gate) '\n   100\t                      f'request {len(it[\"system\"]) + len(it[\"user\"]) + len(json.dumps(it[\"schema\"]))} chars')\n   101\t    (out / 'BUILD.txt').write_text('\\n'.join(report) + '\\n')\n   102\t    print('\\n'.join(report))\n   103\t\n   104\t\n   105\tWRITERS = ('claude', 'codex')\n   106\t_FENCE = re.compile(r'^\\s*```(?:json)?\\s*\\n(.*)\\n\\s*```\\s*$', re.S)\n   107\t\n   108\t\n   109\tdef first_json(text):\n   110\t    \"\"\"[54] The writer's first output exactly as returned: one JSON object, optionally inside a single ```json fence; anything else\n   111\t    (a preface, an array, two objects) is not an answer.\"\"\"\n   112\t    m = _FENCE.match(text)\n   113\t    body = m.group(1) if m else text\n   114\t    data = json.loads(body)\n   115\t    return data if isinstance(data, dict) else None\n   116\t\n   117\t\n   118\tdef inventory(out):\n   119\t    \"\"\"[54] Every registered case has one first answer from each writer.\"\"\"\n   120\t    return [f'{name}/{w}' for name in CASES for w in WRITERS if not (out / name / 'answers' / f'{w}.json').exists()]\n   121\t\n   122\t\n   123\tdef check(out):\n   124\t    missing = inventory(out)\n   125\t    if missing:\n   126\t        raise SystemExit(f'INCOMPLETE: no first answer for {\", \".join(missing)}')\n   127\t    rows = []\n   128\t    for name in CASES:\n   129\t        it = json.loads((out / name / 'item.json').read_text())\n   130\t        for w in WRITERS:\n   131\t            raw = (out / name / 'answers' / f'{w}.json').read_text()\n   132\t            row = {'case': name, 'writer': w, 'sha256': hashlib.sha256(raw.encode()).hexdigest()}\n   133\t            try:\n   134\t                data = first_json(raw)\n   135\t            except json.JSONDecodeError:\n   136\t                data = None\n   137\t            if data is None:\n   138\t                row.update(stage='not JSON', errors=[['format', 'not one JSON object as returned']])\n   139\t            else:\n   140\t                schema_errors = model.check_schema(data, it['schema'])\n   141\t                if schema_errors:\n   142\t                    row.update(stage='schema', errors=[['schema', e] for e in schema_errors])\n   143\t                else:\n   144\t                    try:\n   145\t                        calc = cs.from_answer(data, it['family'])\n   146\t                        result = cs.check(it['family'], it['passages'], calc)\n   147\t                        row.update(stage='checked', errors=[list(e) for e in result['errors']], recorded=result['recorded'],\n   148\t                                   published=result['published'], decision=cs.publish_decision(it['family'], calc, result))\n   149\t                    except Exception as error:                     # [54] recorded per answer, classed apart from the writer's errors\n   150\t                        row.update(stage='checker error', errors=[['checker', f'{type(error).__name__}: {error}'[:300]]])\n   151\t            rows.append(row)\n   152\t    (out / 'CHECKED.json').write_text(json.dumps(rows, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))\n   153\t    for r in rows:\n   154\t        print(f'{r[\"case\"]:5} {r[\"writer\"]:10} {r[\"stage\"]:8} {r.get(\"decision\", \"-\"):9} ' + '; '.join(f'{c}: {d}' for c, d in r['errors'])[:300])\n   155\t\n   156\t\n   157\tREADER_BRIEF = \"\"\"# Blind reading (judging-v13s blind test, SMALL-DESIGN.md §5)\n   158\t\n   159\tYou are given one forecasting request (the questions, their ladders, and every passage the writer was shown) and one answer to it,\n   160\twritten in a JSON format. You are not told who wrote the answer or whether any check accepted it. Read only what is given here.\n   161\t\n   162\tFor **every member** the answer forecasts, and for the answer as a whole, return JSON:\n   163\t\n   164\t{\"members\": {\"<view id>\": {\"supported\": \"yes|no\", \"ground\": \"<the passage ids or the stated assumption that put the forecast in its band>\",\n   165\t                           \"why_not\": \"<if no: what is missing or wrong>\"}},\n   166\t \"defects\": [{\"type\": \"<one of: number misread | wrong arithmetic | part above or added into its whole | two forecasts of one quarter |\n   167\t               own estimate passed off as the market's reference | broken structure>\", \"figures\": [\"<figure ids>\"], \"detail\": \"...\"}]}\n   168\t\n   169\tDefinitions:\n   170\t- supported: the forecast follows from the shown passages and the answer's stated assumptions; a reader could check it against them.\n   171\t- number misread: a source figure's number, scale, sign or qualifier differs from what its passage writes.\n   172\t- wrong arithmetic: a computed figure does not equal its operation on its inputs.\n   173\t- part above or added into its whole: a segment is larger than the total it belongs to, or is added again into a total that already\n   174\t  includes it (directly or through an intermediate figure or an estimate).\n   175\t- two forecasts of one quarter: two different figures are used as the value of one quantity and period. A growth rate computed from\n   176\t  guidance and used only as a stated benchmark for an estimate is not a second value, when one figure supplies the quarter in the\n   177\t  calculation (a ruling). Look through any rate or multiple, including inside a stated assumption, for a second dollar value\n   178\t  of the quarter.\n   179\t- own estimate passed off as the market's reference: a figure marked as the market's reference is, or rests on, the writer's own\n   180\t  estimate or forecast. A reference that applies a past period's reported share or multiple to another period (a quarter's mix\n   181\t  applied to the year) is our comparison estimate, not the market's (a ruling).\n   182\t- broken structure: a link that does not resolve, a figure that depends on itself, a missing or doubled answer, an outcome that is not\n   183\t  the question's quantity, or a rung whose band does not hold the outcome. A total used for a narrower quantity (total capital\n   184\t  expenditure for data-center spending) without a stated deduction or a supported bound is an outcome not of the question's quantity\n   185\t  (a ruling).\n   186\tReturn an empty \"defects\" list when you find none. Return only JSON.\n   187\t\"\"\"\n   188\t\n   189\t\n   190\tdef packets(out):\n   191\t    if inventory(out):\n   192\t        raise SystemExit('INCOMPLETE: packets need every first answer')\n   193\t    rows = json.loads((out / 'CHECKED.json').read_text())\n   194\t    if len(rows) != len(CASES) * len(WRITERS):\n   195\t        raise SystemExit(f'INCOMPLETE: {len(rows)} checked answers, {len(CASES) * len(WRITERS)} registered')\n   196\t    rng = random.Random(hashlib.sha256((out / 'CHECKED.json').read_bytes()).hexdigest())\n   197\t    order = list(range(len(rows)))\n   198\t    rng.shuffle(order)\n   199\t    key = {}\n   200\t    folder = out / 'reader-packets'\n   201\t    folder.mkdir(exist_ok=False)\n   202\t    for n, i in enumerate(order, 1):\n   203\t        r = rows[i]\n   204\t        it = json.loads((out / r['case'] / 'item.json').read_text())\n   205\t        raw = (out / r['case'] / 'answers' / f'{r[\"writer\"]}.json').read_text()\n   206\t        pid = f'R{n:02d}'\n   207\t        key[pid] = {'case': r['case'], 'writer': r['writer']}\n   208\t        (folder / f'{pid}.md').write_text(READER_BRIEF + '\\n# The request as the writer saw it\\n\\n' + it['user'] + '\\n\\n# The answer\\n\\n' + raw + '\\n')\n   209\t    (out / 'reader-key.json').write_text(json.dumps(key, indent=1))\n   210\t    print(f'{len(order)} packets in {folder}; key in reader-key.json (keep from readers)')\n   211\t\n   212\t\n   213\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n   214\t    cmd = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else ''\n   215\t    if cmd in ('build', 'check', 'packets') and len(sys.argv) == 3:\n   216\t        {'build': build, 'check': check, 'packets': packets}[cmd](Path(sys.argv[2]))\n   217\t    else:\n   218\t        raise SystemExit(__doc__)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && nl -ba BLIND3-RESULT.md && nl -ba SMALL-DESIGN.md | sed -n '220,320p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && nl -ba BLIND3-RESULT.md && nl -ba SMALL-DESIGN.md | sed -n '220,320p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# judging-v13s blind test, third run after D742: result (SMALL-DESIGN.md §5 [D742])\n     2\t\n     3\t**STOP on one registered line, as written:** \"an accepted reply with a named defect (marked by both readers …)\".\n     4\t- **R01 (S, Claude writer).** Both readers marked \"broken structure\" on F14: the outcome is a range of $679.25–745B, and rung 4\n     5\t  ($700–800B) does not hold all of it.\n     6\t- **Both adjudicators reject that mark.** The schema the writer was given says the rung is \"for a range outcome, a band it overlaps,\n     7\t  with the reason in reasons\". The answer gives that reason: \"the midpoint and most of the range lie in rung 4\". The code (S6) checks\n     8\t  overlap.\n     9\t- **The cause is my reader brief.** Its definition of broken structure reads \"a rung whose band does not hold the outcome\", without the\n    10\t  schema's range clause. Both readers applied the brief as written. No earlier run had a range that crossed a rung edge, so the gap was\n    11\t  not exercised before.\n    12\t\n    13\tEverything else in the run is clean:\n    14\t- **Writers:** 12 of 12 schema-valid, 12 of 12 accepted, 0 refusals, so there was no refusal review.\n    15\t- **Readers and adjudicators:** six packets drew a disagreement. Every disputed mark was settled, and every one was rejected by both\n    16\t  adjudicators. No defect was upheld, and no split remains.\n    17\t- **Every case has a usable reply.** The joint case has both forecasts supported in one reply (R02 and R11).\n    18\t- **The D742 rule was followed by every P-family writer.** All six recorded the Q4 pace as an estimate naming its benchmark, then\n    19\t  computed Q4 from it. None computed a guidance rate straight into the calculation.\n    20\t\n    21\t**Run:** `poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/`, $0 at the provider. All Codex writers read only `system.txt`, `user.txt` and\n    22\t`schema.json`. The tally is in `TALLY.json`.\n    23\t\n    24\t## 1. Writers' first answers (`CHECKED.json`)\n    25\t\n    26\t| Case | Claude writer | Codex writer |\n    27\t|---|---|---|\n    28\t| P (joint) | v4 416.3, v8 386.1, both rung 2 | v4 420.9, v8 391.0, both rung 2 |\n    29\t| P-v4 | 419.3, rung 2 | 416.3, rung 2 |\n    30\t| P-v8 | 387.4, rung 2 | 388.1, rung 2 |\n    31\t| S (CY2026) | 679.25–745, rung 4 | 670.5, rung 3 |\n    32\t| O | 9–20, rung 1 | 16, rung 1 |\n    33\t| E | 37, rung 3 | 34, rung 3 |\n    34\t\n    35\t## 2. Readers and adjudicators (`TALLY.json`)\n    36\t\n    37\t**Settled as not defects (both adjudicators reject):**\n    38\t- R01 broken structure (both readers' marks), explained above;\n    39\t- R01 \"two forecasts\" (Microsoft backed out of the four-company tallies, a reader matter through `rests_on`);\n    40\t- three \"plus or minus 2%\" midpoints (R02, R09) and a rounding difference within tolerance (R08);\n    41\t- R06's \"number misread\" claims on the $18B schedule and the Lancium tranche.\n    42\t\n    43\t**Support:**\n    44\t- **R07 (S, Codex writer) is settled \"not supported\".** Its rung rests on a 90% data-center share, while the passages put the share near\n    45\t  100%:\n    46\t  - e1947: more than $730B \"on AI infrastructure\" against $720–745B of capex;\n    47\t  - e2759 and e5376: NVIDIA's \"nearly $800 billion\" for the top five, written both as capex and as data-center capex;\n    48\t  - Meta's own figures: about 96%.\n    49\t  At 94% or more, the same $745B gives rung 4. The reply is accepted and publishable, but its rung does not follow from the evidence.\n    50\t  This is not a registered stop line (usable is counted per case, and S has R01). It is a real judgement error in an answer that would\n    51\t  publish.\n    52\t- **R06 (O, Claude writer) is split again** on the $18B reading: Codex says not supported, Claude says supported. This is the same\n    53\t  passage as in both earlier runs.\n    54\t- Every other forecast is supported by both readers or both adjudicators.\n    55\t\n    56\t## 3. What the test shows\n    57\t\n    58\t- **The writer-side contract holds.** In three runs, the request has moved from 11 of 12 accepted with a checker error (run 1), to 11 of\n    59\t  12 with a request contradiction (run 2), to 12 of 12 with no refusal (run 3). D742's rule was followed by all six writers it applies\n    60\t  to.\n    61\t- **The stop this time is in the measuring instrument.** The reader brief's definition is narrower than the format the writer was\n    62\t  given. Both adjudicators corrected it from the format rule.\n    63\t- **The readers did their job on substance.** They found the one reply whose decisive assumption is unsupported (R07). That is the\n    64\t  kind of error the paid re-send is meant to measure in gpt-6-luna.\n    65\t- **Open disclosures:**\n    66\t  - O's $18B reading (split three runs running);\n    67\t  - wrong numbers in prose, which this run's adjudications did not raise;\n    68\t  - R07's unsupported share.\n   220\t  - a point Data Center forecast beside a company range (S3 holds);\n   221\t  - a final range estimate resting on a computed point of the same quantity (S4 holds).\n   222\t- **A2 adds:**\n   223\t  - Data Center × 1x added to company (S8);\n   224\t  - an estimate resting on both part and whole (recorded, not refused, and the record asserted);\n   225\t  - two Data Center Q4 figures on two paths (S4);\n   226\t  - Q3 guidance used directly beside a Q3 forecast (S4);\n   227\t  - an estimate itself marked as the reference (S5);\n   228\t  - a computed reference with basis forecast (S5);\n   229\t  - a declared value within tolerance whose recomputed value crosses the rung edge (S6 on the recomputed value);\n   230\t  - a part whose recomputed lowest value exceeds the whole's recomputed highest, while its declared value does not (S3);\n   231\t  - sum($108B, 2%) (S2 unit);\n   232\t  - division by [-1, 1] (S2);\n   233\t  - [-3, -2] × [2, 4] declared other than [-12, -4] (S2);\n   234\t  - a source as the outcome (S6);\n   235\t  - a figure id equal to a passage id (S7);\n   236\t  - \"plus or minus 2%\" copied as \"2%\" and used as +2% for the range (S1);\n   237\t  - a euro amount (S1).\n   238\t- **A3:** each mistake must be refused by the schema or **actually refused** by its stated rule (asserted). \"first half\" is refused by\n   239\t  S8 when summed. \"1.05 USD trillion\" fails the schema, and \"1050 USD bn\" passes.\n   240\t- **A4, the end to end rehearsal.** One v13s reply goes through the first attempt, the separate-arm reconciliation, the card render and\n   241\t  recovery. For each named defect, the defective answer fails its rule while its paired correct answer reaches the reader's card. The\n   242\t  old run's `results.json` reproduces from its journals with the ledger snapshot saved inside it.\n   243\t\n   244\t**[52] Readers.**\n   245\t- **What they get.** Both readers get the same complete shown passages, with the writer's identity and the checker's decision masked.\n   246\t- **What they mark, on every first reply:**\n   247\t  - whether each forecast is supported, naming the passage or assumption that puts it in its band;\n   248\t  - any of D737's five defects;\n   249\t  - broken structure.\n   250\t- **The wording review is separate.** Refusals are revealed only after that marking, for the review of whether the request states\n   251\t  the rule.\n   252\t- **An accepted reply with a named defect** (marked by both readers, or by the third reader) is a stop.\n   253\t- **INCOMPLETE** is judged against the inventory of 12 first replies and 24 readings plus the third readings due.\n   254\t\n   255\t**Part B, blind writers ($0 at the provider).**\n   256\t- **The writers.** Each of the six cases is written once by a fresh Claude subagent and once by a fresh read-only Codex session, 12\n   257\t  sessions in all. Each gets only that case's exact outgoing system text, user text and schema.\n   258\t- **The first outputs** go through `model.check_schema`, `from_answer` and `check` unedited.\n   259\t- **The readers.** Two readers who wrote neither the design nor the answers (a Claude subagent and a Codex session) grade **every**\n   260\t  answer, accepted or refused, against the shown passages. For each answer they record:\n   261\t  - for each refusal, whether the exact request states the condition (the sentence quoted) and whether the answer was right;\n   262\t  - for each accepted answer, whether each forecast is supported, and whether its recorded conversions or estimates decide its band.\n   263\t- **A third reader** settles disagreements.\n   264\t- **Usable** means accepted, publishable by `publish_decision`, and supported by the readers. For the joint case, both forecasts must\n   265\t  be supported in one reply.\n   266\t\n   267\t**Stop.** The test stops on any of these:\n   268\t- an A1 form refused;\n   269\t- an A2 defect not refused by its rule;\n   270\t- an A3 mistake neither impossible nor stated;\n   271\t- a Part B refusal whose condition the request does not state, or that refuses a right answer;\n   272\t- an INCOMPLETE run;\n   273\t- a case with zero usable first replies across both writers;\n   274\t- the joint case without both supported forecasts in one reply.\n   275\t\n   276\t**A clean result** goes to Alex as the request for the paid re-send: the same 36 requests rebuilt in v13s, under a new decision with\n   277\tD725's lines. Only that run measures whether luna can do it.\n   278\t\n   279\t**[D742] Registered before the third run (council rounds 56–56c).** The re-run stopped on one S4 refusal of a sound answer\n   280\t(`BLIND2-RESULT.md`). The cause was the request: the system text said to carry \"the guided growth forward\", while the schema allowed a\n   281\tguidance rate only as \"a stated benchmark for an estimate\" and the header required every path to go through the forecast. S4 is\n   282\tunchanged (rounds 56 and 56b showed that both a blanket and a narrowed exemption let a reset to guidance publish). The request now states\n   283\tone rule in the system text, the schema and the header: guidance informs the pace; the forecast pace is recorded as an estimate that\n   284\tnames its benchmark in `rests_on`; the quarter's dollar value is the one forecast figure. The rules for the third run:\n   285\t- **The stop lines are unchanged.**\n   286\t- **The refusal review** records two judgements apart for each refusal:\n   287\t  - sound: is the forecast and its reasoning financially sound?\n   288\t  - stated: does the exact request (system text, schema and user text) clearly state the condition?\n   289\t  A sound answer refused under a clearly stated condition still stops the run.\n   290\t- **The readers' brief** keeps Alex's ruling-1 sentence and adds: \"Look through any rate or multiple, including inside a stated\n   291\t  assumption, for a second dollar value of the quarter.\"\n   292\t- **Adjudication:**\n   293\t  - Where the two readers disagree, two adjudicators, one per family, read the packet. The packet now includes the system text.\n   294\t  - A point is settled when both agree.\n   295\t  - A settled defect on an accepted reply is a stop.\n   296\t  - A split is disclosed, not a stop.\n   297\t- **What each outcome sends where:**\n   298\t  - a fresh sound refusal sends the format back to council;\n   299\t  - an accepted reply confirmed to carry two values of a quarter sends the publication rule back to council;\n   300\t  - only a complete run that meets every line goes to Alex for the paid re-send.\n   301\t- **Part A for the change:**\n   302\t  - five new cases: the stated-estimate benchmark passes; four forms of the saved refusal or a guidance reset are refused by S4;\n   303\t  - one new mutant: S4's walk following `rests_on` must fail the stated-estimate case;\n   304\t  - `s4_replay.py` on the saved reply.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && nl -ba blind_adjudicate.py | sed -n '1,300p' && rg -n 'def v13s_schema|band it overlaps|S6' render_v13.py calc_small.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba AGENTS.md | sed -n '310,380p' && nl -ba docs/CURRENT_STATE.md | sed -n '433,480p' && tail -16 docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && nl -ba blind_adjudicate.py | sed -n '1,300p' && rg -n 'def v13s_schema|band it overlaps|S6' render_v13.py calc_small.py\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t\"\"\"Adjudication and refusal-review packets for a judging-v13s blind test (SMALL-DESIGN.md §5, D742).\n     2\t\n     3\tAdjudication: for every reply whose two readers disagree (a member's \"supported\", or any defect one reader marks), one packet holding\n     4\tthe two readings, the system text, the format rules the writer was given (every schema description), the request as the writer saw it\n     5\tand the answer. Reader 1 is the Codex reading and Reader 2 the Claude reading; the adjudicators are not told which.\n     6\t\n     7\tRefusal review: for every refused first reply, one packet with the refusal messages, the system text, the schema, the user text and the\n     8\tanswer, asking the two registered judgements apart: is the forecast and its reasoning financially sound, and does the exact request\n     9\tclearly state the condition the refusal enforces (D742: a sound answer refused under a clearly stated condition still stops the run).\n    10\t\n    11\tUsage: python3 blind_adjudicate.py <blind test folder> <packet id> [<packet id> ...]\n    12\t       python3 blind_adjudicate.py refusal <blind test folder> <case> <writer>\n    13\t\"\"\"\n    14\timport json\n    15\timport sys\n    16\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    17\t\n    18\tHEADER = \"\"\"# Adjudication (judging-v13s blind test)\n    19\t\n    20\tTwo readers disagreed about the answer below. Settle each point against the passages in the request and the format rules quoted\n    21\tbelow, not against either reader's threshold. Read only what is given here.\n    22\t\n    23\tFor each member, decide **supported** (yes or no): the forecast follows from the shown passages and the answer's stated assumptions.\n    24\tFor each defect a reader marked, decide **uphold** or **reject**, quoting the passage words or the format rule that decides it. The\n    25\tdefect types are:\n    26\t- number misread: a source figure's number, scale, sign or qualifier differs from what its passage's quote writes, allowing what the\n    27\t  format rules permit.\n    28\t- wrong arithmetic: a computed figure does not equal its operation on its inputs.\n    29\t- part above or added into its whole: a segment is larger than the total it belongs to, or is added again into a total that already\n    30\t  includes it.\n    31\t- two forecasts of one quarter: two different figures are used as the value of one quantity and period. A growth rate computed from\n    32\t  guidance and used only as a stated benchmark for an estimate is not a second value, when one figure supplies the quarter in the\n    33\t  calculation (a ruling). Look through any rate or multiple, including inside a stated assumption, for a second dollar value\n    34\t  of the quarter.\n    35\t- own estimate passed off as the market's reference: a figure marked as the market's reference is, or rests on, the writer's own\n    36\t  estimate or forecast. A reference that applies a past period's reported share or multiple to another period (a quarter's mix\n    37\t  applied to the year) is our comparison estimate, not the market's (a ruling).\n    38\t- broken structure: a link that does not resolve, a figure depending on itself, a missing or doubled answer, an outcome not of the\n    39\t  question's quantity, a rung whose band does not hold the outcome. A total used for a narrower quantity (total capital expenditure\n    40\t  for data-center spending) without a stated deduction or a supported bound is an outcome not of the question's quantity (a ruling).\n    41\t\n    42\tReturn only JSON: {\"members\": {\"<view id>\": {\"supported\": \"yes|no\", \"why\": \"...\"}},\n    43\t \"defects\": [{\"reader\": \"Reader 1|Reader 2\", \"type\": \"...\", \"figures\": [...], \"decision\": \"uphold|reject\", \"why\": \"...\"}]}\n    44\t\"\"\"\n    45\t\n    46\t\n    47\tdef descriptions(schema, path=''):\n    48\t    \"\"\"Every description in the schema, keyed by its field path.\"\"\"\n    49\t    found = {}\n    50\t    if isinstance(schema, dict):\n    51\t        if isinstance(schema.get('description'), str):\n    52\t            found[path.strip('/') or 'answer'] = schema['description']\n    53\t        for key, value in schema.items():\n    54\t            if key != 'description':\n    55\t                step = '' if key in ('properties', 'items', 'anyOf') else key\n    56\t                found.update(descriptions(value, f'{path}/{step}' if step else path))\n    57\t    elif isinstance(schema, list):\n    58\t        for value in schema:\n    59\t            found.update(descriptions(value, path))\n    60\t    return found\n    61\t\n    62\t\n    63\tdef reading_lines(label, reading):\n    64\t    lines = []\n    65\t    for member, mark in sorted(reading.get('members', {}).items()):\n    66\t        line = f\"- {label} on member {member}: supported = {mark.get('supported')}. Ground: {mark.get('ground', '')}\"\n    67\t        if mark.get('why_not'):\n    68\t            line += f\" Why not: {mark['why_not']}\"\n    69\t        lines.append(line)\n    70\t    defects = reading.get('defects', [])\n    71\t    if not defects:\n    72\t        lines.append(f'- {label} marks no defect.')\n    73\t    for defect in defects:\n    74\t        lines.append(f\"- {label} marks a defect: {defect.get('type')} (figures {defect.get('figures', [])}): {defect.get('detail', '')}\")\n    75\t    return lines\n    76\t\n    77\t\n    78\tdef build(folder, packet_ids):\n    79\t    key = json.loads((folder / 'reader-key.json').read_text())\n    80\t    out = folder / 'adjudication'\n    81\t    out.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n    82\t    for pid in packet_ids:\n    83\t        case, writer = key[pid]['case'], key[pid]['writer']\n    84\t        codex = json.loads((folder / 'reader-packets' / f'{pid}.codex.json').read_text())\n    85\t        claude = json.loads((folder / 'reader-packets' / f'{pid}.claude.json').read_text())\n    86\t        schema = json.loads((folder / case / 'schema.json').read_text())\n    87\t        text = '\\n'.join([HEADER, '# The two readings', *reading_lines('Reader 1', codex), *reading_lines('Reader 2', claude), '',\n    88\t                          '# The system text the writer was given', (folder / case / 'system.txt').read_text(), '',\n    89\t                          '# The format rules the writer was given (schema descriptions)',\n    90\t                          json.dumps(descriptions(schema), indent=1, ensure_ascii=False), '',\n    91\t                          '# The request (questions, ladders and every passage)', (folder / case / 'user.txt').read_text(), '',\n    92\t                          '# The answer', (folder / case / 'answers' / f'{writer}.json').read_text()])\n    93\t        target = out / f'{pid}.md'\n    94\t        if target.exists():\n    95\t            raise SystemExit(f'{target} exists')\n    96\t        target.write_text(text)\n    97\t        (out / f'{pid}.prompt.txt').write_text(f'Read the file {target} and nothing else (no other file, no web). Follow its '\n    98\t                                               'instructions and return only the JSON it asks for.\\n')\n    99\t        print(f'{pid}: {case}/{writer}, {len(text)} chars')\n   100\t\n   101\t\n   102\tREFUSAL_HEADER = \"\"\"# Refusal review (judging-v13s blind test)\n   103\t\n   104\tA code check refused the answer below. For each refusal message, give two judgements apart, from the request text and the passages\n   105\talone:\n   106\t1. sound: is the forecast and its reasoning financially sound against the passages (would an analyst accept the number and the reasons\n   107\t   that produce it)? Judge this on its own, apart from the format rule the check enforces. Answer yes or no, with why.\n   108\t2. stated: does the exact request (system text, schema or user text below) clearly state the condition the refusal enforces? Answer\n   109\t   yes or no, and quote the sentence that states it, or say none does.\n   110\tReturn only JSON: {\"refusals\": [{\"message\": \"...\", \"sound\": \"yes|no\", \"why\": \"...\", \"stated\": \"yes|no\", \"sentence\": \"...\"}]}\n   111\t\"\"\"\n   112\t\n   113\t\n   114\tdef refusal(folder, case, writer):\n   115\t    checked = {(r['case'], r['writer']): r for r in json.loads((folder / 'CHECKED.json').read_text())}\n   116\t    row = checked[(case, writer)]\n   117\t    if row.get('decision') == 'publish' or not row.get('errors'):\n   118\t        raise SystemExit(f'{case}/{writer} was not refused')\n   119\t    out = folder / 'refusal-review'\n   120\t    out.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n   121\t    text = '\\n'.join([REFUSAL_HEADER, '# Refusal messages', json.dumps(row['errors'], ensure_ascii=False), '',\n   122\t                      '# The system text', (folder / case / 'system.txt').read_text(), '',\n   123\t                      '# The schema', (folder / case / 'schema.json').read_text(), '',\n   124\t                      '# The user text (the request, with every passage)', (folder / case / 'user.txt').read_text(), '',\n   125\t                      '# The answer', (folder / case / 'answers' / f'{writer}.json').read_text()])\n   126\t    target = out / f'{case}-{writer}.md'\n   127\t    if target.exists():\n   128\t        raise SystemExit(f'{target} exists')\n   129\t    target.write_text(text)\n   130\t    (out / f'{case}-{writer}.prompt.txt').write_text(f'Read the file {target} and nothing else (no other file, no web). Follow its '\n   131\t                                                    'instructions and return only the JSON it asks for.\\n')\n   132\t    print(f'refusal review {case}/{writer}: {len(text)} chars')\n   133\t\n   134\t\n   135\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n   136\t    if len(sys.argv) == 5 and sys.argv[1] == 'refusal':\n   137\t        refusal(Path(sys.argv[2]).resolve(), sys.argv[3], sys.argv[4])\n   138\t    elif len(sys.argv) >= 3 and sys.argv[1] != 'refusal':\n   139\t        build(Path(sys.argv[1]).resolve(), sys.argv[2:])\n   140\t    else:\n   141\t        raise SystemExit(__doc__)\nrender_v13.py:81:def v13s_schema(member_ids, evidence_ids, theme_ids):\nrender_v13.py:145:                          '(a band includes its lower edge, not its upper); for a range outcome, a band it overlaps, with the reason in reasons.'}),\ncalc_small.py:3:quarter, S5 an own estimate passed off as the market's) and for broken structure (S6, S7), and only where the calculation's own\ncalc_small.py:162:    `reference`; marker errors go in `decode_errors` (S5, S6, S7). An empty string counts as absent.\"\"\"\ncalc_small.py:193:                errors.append(('S6', f'{v}: {len(outs)} figures are marked as its outcome; exactly one is required'))\ncalc_small.py:562:            errors.append(('S6', f'{v}: its outcome {out[\"id\"]} must be your own forecast (a computed or estimate figure with basis forecast)'))\ncalc_small.py:564:            errors.append(('S6', f'{v}: outcome {out[\"id\"]} measures {\" | \".join(_key(out[\"what\"]))}, not the question\\'s {\" | \".join(_key(member[\"what\"]))}'))\ncalc_small.py:566:            errors.append(('S6', f'{v}: outcome {out[\"id\"]} is in {out[\"unit\"]}, not {member.get(\"unit\", \"USD bn\")}'))\ncalc_small.py:570:            errors.append(('S6', f'{v}: rung {rung!r} is not one of 1..{len(member[\"bands\"])}'))\ncalc_small.py:575:            errors.append(('S6', f'{v}: rung {rung} {member[\"bands\"][rung - 1]} does not hold its outcome {shown} as recomputed'))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba AGENTS.md | sed -n '310,380p' && nl -ba docs/CURRENT_STATE.md | sed -n '433,480p' && tail -16 docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md\"","aggregated_output":"   310\t- **Measure end to end before a step's arm, and read the parked designs first.** A step's noise that the next step removes is not the\n   311\t  defect, and a step's recall that the next step throws away is. Before any arm on one step: the production replay through the whole path\n   312\t  on the gold window, the count at the step the product reads, and the decisions on the topic read for a parked fix (Alex, 2026-10-31:\n   313\t  \"make sure we are not going around in circles using wrong ruler and wrong prompts that don't work\"). Before a phase targets one step,\n   314\t  the upside of that step done perfectly is measured where the product is judged: the judge is given the gold's own evidence, built by\n   315\t  the production code, a few sends (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"我很不开心你的失败，为什么，深度多轮检讨记录，想思路突破\").\n   316\t- **Read what was kept against the gold, blind, before the next noise arm.** The not-kept gold entries a version keeps are judged by a\n   317\t  reader who wrote neither the gold nor the prompt, mixed with controls it cannot tell apart; where it parts from the gold, the standard\n   318\t  is unclear or the gold misreads it, and that goes to Alex before any arm counts it as noise (Alex, 2026-10-31: \"你再次重新检查尺子，看看是不是这些留下的还有歧义；然后再思考怎么降低noise\").\n   319\t- Pair every structural check with its semantic one. Run a data rule over its whole input range and on cases it was not tuned on. Weigh\n   320\t  a case by what it carries in the product, not by count.\n   321\t- A claim about a population (\"the data is clean\") rests on a code sweep of the whole population and an independent read of a fresh\n   322\t  random sample, never on the pages the author looked at.\n   323\t- Cost is priced from tokens at the published rates (`hivemind.model.PRICES`, cached input at `model.CACHED_INPUT_SHARE`), never from a\n   324\t  stored `cost_usd`; say which rates a projection uses.\n   325\t\n   326\t### 7.3 Iterating\n   327\t\n   328\t- **One class at a time** (Alex, 2026-10-29: \"你一类一类改，快速迭代然后测regression\"). Count the misses by mechanism; take the largest\n   329\t  class; trace it to the sentence that causes it; change one thing aimed at that class; run the whole bench (a prompt change alters every\n   330\t  request) against the previous version; read every regression to its raw answer. The pages that showed the failure locate its\n   331\t  mechanism; only the whole bench (every set, every draw) accepts the change.\n   332\t- **Name the effect on the judgement first.** Every proposed change states the effect it is expected to have on a reader or on the final\n   333\t  judgement, and is tested there where possible; a step's own counts do not decide it alone. A fix that keeps moving its error to\n   334\t  neighbouring cases stops being tuned on that set (Alex, 2026-11-09: \"感觉现在一直在修一些mknor的原地打转，你是不是要思考下现在具体还差什么high priority big impact 的需要做？\";\n   335\t  he approved this rule the same day, D391).\n   336\t- **A model call is a sampler.** Re-send a stored request before calling its answer a defect. Totals and acceptance come from at least\n   337\t  three samples beside a fresh control; a bar the control fails against itself judges nothing. A direct-read pass\n   338\t  (one send per article, every answer read beside its source; D238) locates mechanisms; its counts are one draw and are labelled so.\n   339\t- **A written log.** One row per arm: hypothesis, change, numbers against the control (regressions first), kept or not. Refuted arms and\n   340\t  your own mistakes stay in it; the next session starts from its last row.\n   341\t- **Own the loop, within what Alex agreed.** When the direction is agreed and no stop is in force (`CURRENT_STATE.md`), push your own\n   342\t  hypotheses through $0 checks and probes of a few cents on stored cases without asking. A registered test, an end-to-end run, or\n   343\t  anything that departs from the agreed plan starts on his word; a result that contradicts the hypothesis stops the line and goes to him\n   344\t  (D355: \"如果有什么不符合hypothesis 的地方你需要终止然后和我说我们重新评估\"). While he is not active (D439), \"his word\" is the council's\n   345\t  recorded consensus, and a stopped line goes to the council for re-assessment.\n   346\t- **Council before every change is sent.** A prompt, schema, code or criterion change, including one found by reading a probe, is a new\n   347\t  arm. It goes to an independent Codex read and a challenge round before its first send, and its result goes to a challenge round\n   348\t  before the next change. Reading the traces and the model's own account locates a fix; it does not review it (Alex, 2026-11-08:\n   349\t  \"你这些改动有我你有好好的跑council 再下手\").\n   350\t  Every round's reasoning and decisions are reflected on in the council until there is a consensus; the decision is recorded, and\n   351\t  the next test goes straight ahead, held to the PRD and its quantified goals, with every trace read by you yourself and not only\n   352\t  by readers (Alex, 2026-11-10: \"你应该跑council loop 来reflect 你每一轮的思路还有决策，需要你打成共识，记录决策，向前直行测试。不要drift,我们有PRD和量化目标，\n   353\t  你自己作为llm 下去看所有trace\").\n   354\t- **Small first, then one run.** A hypothesis is first validated the simplest way, on a few stored cases and a few cents, and shown to\n   355\t  work at a high level before any full analysis or stability test is built (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"don't overspend resources on wasting time.\n   356\t  We need to validate the hypothesis in a very simple way and to make sure that it works on a high level before we dive into do the full\n   357\t  analysis stability test. This is a principle you should remember\"). A day or week slice before any whole-corpus run; preflight on\n   358\t  stored data before any paid run (§5); no edit while a run is live (§9). A paid run measures a configuration; it never tries a fix.\n   359\t  Before each send, write what it can still change in the decision and which risk the cheaper check left uncovered; a replicate or\n   360\t  control that only re-measures noise or a settled comparison is not sent, and a fix is not sent before the model's own account and the\n   361\t  request locate where the decision is made (Alex, 2026-10-30: \"你跑这么多次真的有意义吗\"; \"我感觉你在为了跑而跑\"). Several fixes on one\n   362\t  base are each proved on stored data in minutes and then run together once (Alex, 2026-11-02: \"快速验证。不要drift,不要跑超级繁琐的全方位验证，先poc 改，能work,有结论，全部改动放到一起再跑完整\"; D266).\n   363\t- **One recommendation, one test.** What reaches Alex as the next step of work is one recommendation and one test of it, reached after\n   364\t  rounds of review (Claude's own, Codex's, an independent reader's) on the traces until a round finds nothing serious; never a menu of\n   365\t  arms or options, never a conclusion the next probe overturns (a choice that changes what the system does still goes to him with its\n   366\t  options and a recommendation, Authority and scope) (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"就测试一种，一次 … 你就没有自己看5轮review，能不能自己有个超级自信的定论和证据再给我提建议？\").\n   367\t  An agreed recommendation is first challenged by an independent reader on the concrete evidence behind it (\"why you give\n   368\t  recommendations for this. What did you see exactly?\"). A review round reads a rule as its author meant it; only a send shows how the\n   369\t  model applies it: before a registered test, the changed request is sent on the cases that motivated it, a few cents.\n   370\t- **A failed arm is diagnosed before the next one.** When an arm fixes its class and regresses another, write the root cause first: the\n   371\t  process error (what grew, what the small sample did not guard) and the mechanism, traced to the raw answers and the model's account,\n   372\t  never a guess stated as the cause. A small sample guards every class the change can move, not only its own. When a fix keeps moving\n   373\t  another class, the call is doing several jobs: move the rule to its owner (a field's definition sits in the schema beside the field)\n   374\t  rather than add a sentence (Alex, 2026-10-30: \"那你这些修改都是失败的呀，为什么，根因，你要检讨然后再接着尝试。我觉得你已经陷入deep loop 了\").\n   375\t  A failed step of a plan is fixed and re-run at that same step: its failures are the work list, and nothing later in the plan and no\n   376\t  substitute plan starts before it passes (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"你为什么要drift? 你现在明明还有这么多的问题要fix,你到底知不知道你要fix什么？\").\n   377\t  Before a fix is proposed, write which goal the mechanism still serves and what the product already gives for it; a measurement that\n   378\t  removes the reason a mechanism exists retires the mechanism instead of starting its repair (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"I told you to think about\n   379\t  it and you're giving me suggestions that you reject yourself\").\n   380\t- **Before a version is rejected, the rejection is checked.** Every failed or refused answer behind a \"did not pass\" is read against its\n   433\t**The merge test (D678–D680, 2026-11-19): closed; the registered test did not pass.** The old system opens questions, clean Step 1 reads\n   434\tand files under them, and the frozen judge answers. It ran on 70 articles × old-2 and old-3, with a hybrid arm and a control arm, for\n   435\t$2.13 ([result](research/2026-11-19-merge-council/RESULT.md)).\n   436\t- **Held:**\n   437\t  - delivery: the decisive statements reached the judge on 4/4 primary questions in both draws;\n   438\t  - talks stayed talks;\n   439\t  - both blind readers supported all 4 hybrid answers;\n   440\t  - no five-company or 2027 figure was taken as the answer;\n   441\t  - c8 proposed no NVIDIA-figure question.\n   442\t- **Missed:**\n   443\t  - P2's proxy clause: total capex is used for data-center capex without being named a proxy, which old also misses;\n   444\t  - V: the rebuilt control's v47 was unsupported, and a reconstruction effect is not ruled out.\n   445\t- **Not shown:** that the merge answers better. The old answers were already supported, and the capex band was set by 09-06 history.\n   446\t- **Next:** superseded by D681, below.\n   447\t\n   448\t**The one next task: run the third v13s blind test (12 fresh writers, then readers, reviewers and adjudicators) on the request D742\n   449\tfixed, and score it on the registered lines (`research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md` §5 [D742]).**\n   450\t\n   451\t- **The re-run stopped on one line** (D742, `research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND2-RESULT.md`).\n   452\t  - S4 refused a sound answer that computed a guidance growth rate straight into Q4.\n   453\t  - 12 of 12 were schema-valid and 11 of 12 accepted. Every case was usable. No defect was settled.\n   454\t- **The cause was the request.** The system text invited carrying the guided growth forward directly, while the schema and S4 allow a\n   455\t  guidance rate only as an estimate's benchmark (Alex's ruling 1 as written).\n   456\t- **Council 56–56c.** A blanket exemption and a narrowed exemption each let a reset to guidance publish. So S4 stays, and the request\n   457\t  states one rule in three places: guidance informs the pace; the pace is an estimate naming its benchmark; the quarter's dollar value\n   458\t  is the one forecast figure.\n   459\t- **Checks:** cases 109 of 109, mutants 42 of 42, rehearsal 19 of 19. The v13 plan hash is unchanged. `s4_replay.py` refuses the saved\n   460\t  reply and both council resets, and passes the stated-estimate form.\n   461\t- **Two reader splits are disclosed, not stops:**\n   462\t  - O's \"$18 billion committed for the remainder of its fiscal year\" reading, which decides O's rung;\n   463\t  - wrong numbers in prose that no figure carries.\n   464\t- **Run folder:** `poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/`.\n   465\t- **What each outcome sends where:**\n   466\t  - a fresh sound refusal, or an accepted reply confirmed to carry two values of a quarter, goes back to council;\n   467\t  - a run meeting every line goes to Alex as the paid re-send request.\n   468\t\n   469\tThe record before D742:\n   470\t\n   471\t**Earlier next task (done, D742): re-run the v13s blind test once with fresh writers and readers, after the reader calibration on\n   472\tAlex's rulings (D740, D741).**\n   473\t\n   474\t- **The first blind test stopped** (D740, `research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND-RESULT.md`):\n   475\t  - 12 of 12 first answers were schema-valid, and 11 of 12 passed every check.\n   476\t  - **Stop 1:** S1 read \"from $35 billion to $170 billion\" as a range. This was Claude's change, now fixed: an \"X to Y\" after \"from\" is a\n   477\t    change between two values.\n   478\t  - **Stop 2:** the readers marked a guidance-implied growth benchmark as \"two forecasts of one quarter\".\n   479\t- **Alex ruled the readers' boundary questions** (D741):\n   480\t  - a guidance-implied growth benchmark is not a defect;\n| 26 | 11-05 凌晨 | 乙的第一步：新闻稿（带表格的原始文字）交给冻结的抽取当开始跟踪时的第一份材料，3 次；独立读者先查过，把\"怎么算过\"改严（数字必须在存下的引用里、并写明是一季度） | 没过：写下 13–21 条（收入、毛利率、每股收益、指引……挂 v1/v2/v3/v11/v7/v8），**营业利润和购置固定资产两行三次都没写**；冻结的抽取只读新闻稿的文字段落、不读后面的财务表格。第二步拿不到起点数，不做 | 在这一步修：每道题单独问一次财报要它自己的起点数（一次只想一道题），原文那行由代码核对，再走冻结的判断 |\n| 27 | 11-05 凌晨 | 乙的第一步第二版：每道题单独读一次新闻稿要起点数（不改冻结提示词，判断那一步的模型设置）；独立读者先查出四处（例子正是两道题的定义、数字比对太松太严、读错列规则误伤、第二版没写下），核实后照改，25 个对照全对、两个故意弄坏的版本都被抓出 | v10 2/3（第 3 次整行照抄被拒，数是对的）、v12 3/3（自己认出资本开支就是\"购置固定资产和无形资产\"那行）；对照 v4 白卷 3/3；对照 v7 照登记没过——2/3 次交回不是数的说明，其中一条因产品名\"A5X\"里的\"5\"被代码收下；修了数字认法，存下的回答重跑只有这两条变成拒收 | 第二步 |\n| 28 | 11-05 凌晨 | 乙的第二步：只用系统自己读到的数，搭 7 月 14 日的冻结判断请求，v10 两份、v12 三份各发一次，按冻结尺子的规则打分 | **v10 判第 2 档 2/2（算上没判的那次 2/3），v12 判第 4 档 3/3，全在读者 B 的范围里**；理由都是用读到的数算的（65.9%；17.57 亿推全年 50–80 亿）。两步合计约 2.5 美分 | 独立读者核对理由、挑战建议；然后报 Alex |\n| 29 | 11-05 凌晨 | 独立读者核对结果、挑战\"直接做进生产再跑 14 天\"的建议 | 判断理由站得住、记录如实（发之前的版本已还原、锁定码对上）；但只测了 2/22 道题，财报里有挨着但不是那个量的数（v20、v9 旁边），而冻结版本已判对 15–16 道；文件是人挑的；\"和存档比\"违反 PRD 10 | 建议撤回；下一步：同样的读法用在全部 22 道种子题，读到数的题在窗口末判断、当天重发对照，已判对的题一道不能变错 |\n| 30 | 11-05 | Alex：\"你充分验证\"。乙的全部 22 道题验证：设计（`baseline-design.md` 第 8 轮）——文件由代码选（开始跟踪前最近一个财报日的财报类材料：5 月 20 日新闻稿和 CFO 说明）；读法和第二版一字不差，每题每份文件 3 次；判断照 PRD 10 §4 当天原样重发：三遍各自拿窗口末最后一次判断的存档请求，对照原样 3 次，起点组只在证据块最前面加上读到的数；过关三条事先写下（v10、v12 各 ≥ 6/9；不弄坏：同一遍里重排的精确检验显著少、或少 2 次以上且两人读理由认定是起点数带偏；读到的数五类分类，读错、别的量、不是数一个都不能有） | 发之前修了两处：读法的检查原来要求\"引用的最后一个数就是读到的数\"，照抄整句的正常引用会被拒（4 句全拒），改成\"读到的数印在引用里\"（对照 32 例全对，两个弄坏的版本分别抓出 5、1 个错；试点重放只有 v10 第 3 次那两条整行变成收下，v10 变 3/3）；发送脚本按冻结尺子补上是非题判法、\"档动了\"对着请求里那次上一次结论查（三遍存档 57 个结论和 `score_judgement.py` 逐题一致，弄坏的判法被抓出）。审查：Codex 4 轮（第 1 轮 5 条严重、第 2 轮 3 条严重，都属实都改；第 3、4 轮无严重问题），独立读者 1 次（请求干净、没有金标泄漏；挪档看不见、单位后缀、口径错等照改） | 设计和 8 个脚本锁定（`baseline-all.sha256`）；发读数 132 次 |\n| 31 | 11-05 | 乙的全部 22 道题验证，照锁定的设计测一次：读 132 次（0.083 美元）、两人分类（第二位盲分）、判断 144 次（0.344 美元），三遍各自和当天原样重发的对照比 | **第 1 条过**：v10、v12 各 9/9 判对。**第 2 条过**：读到数的 7 道判过的题两组选档逐次一样，只有 v22 第 2 遍少 1 次（7/9 对 6/9，理由显示是本来的抽样起伏，起点组写明\"没有把一季度乘 4\"）。**第 3 条没过**：53 个收下的数里 5 个是别的量——v19（Vera CPU 收入）两次收了\"数据中心计算收入 604 亿\"，v20（Blackwell 和 Rubin 收入）两次收了\"数据中心收入 752 亿\"和\"网络收入 148 亿\"；判断都没被带偏（v19 理由写明计算收入里没有单列 Vera CPU） | 照登记停，交 Alex |\n| 32 | 11-05 | 问模型自己为什么收那 5 个数（3 次，约 0.3 美分，`probe-baseline-account.md`） | 3 次都指向读法任务里那一句\"报告没用题目的名字写这个量时，写出组成它的行、或报告记它的那一行\"，并自己说这些数不是这道题的量、不该写。这一句是 v10、v12 要用的，在报告根本没有这个量的题上把模型推去写更大或旁边的行 | 建议：只改这一句的边界（只收\"由它算出的那几行\"和\"换了名字的同一个量\"，更大的、旁边的行不算），按提示词审计改，再在 22 道题上测一次；等 Alex 的话 |\n| 33 | 11-05 | Alex：\"改\"。只改读法里那一句：原句\"写出组成它的行、或报告记它的那一行\"→ 新句\"只写算出它的那几行，或换了名字的同一个量；更大的行、旁边的行都不写\"（任务 790 → 889 字符，理由：抽象说法换成闭合两类加边界）。提示词审计、Codex 只读审 1 轮（1 条严重：发送失败会被当成白卷，已改成\"不完整、不下结论\"）；先在 v19、v20、v10、v12 上试发 24 次（1.6 美分） | 试发过：v19、v20 三次都白卷，v10 3/3；v12 2/3——问模型（2 次）：新句的\"更大的行\"半句让它把\"购置固定资产和无形资产\"当成比资本开支宽的一行，其中一次重想后改口\"就是资本开支\" | 照登记测全部 22 道题 |\n| 34 | 11-05 | 第三版的登记测试：和第 8 轮一样，只换这一句；读 132 次（0.078 美元）、两人分类（第二位盲分）、读到数的 7 道题三遍重判、当天对照（108 次，0.268 美元） | **三条全过**：v10、v12 各 9/9；判对的题一道没变错（只有 v22 第 2 遍反过来对照 0/3、起点组 3/3，理由是在 41% 和 32% 两个增长估计间摇摆，和第 13 轮方向相反，与起点数无关）；46 个数全是自己的量（2 条是标明的二季度指引），两人分类全一致；v19、v20 的错数全没了，其余 15 道白卷、没冒出新错。没盖住：资本开支那一行试发时漏过 1 次；指引也被写成\"事实\"；一路判下来的效果和跨题效果要端到端才量得到 | 交 Alex：要不要做进生产、跑 14 天三遍端到端 |\n| 35 | 11-05 | 独立读者挑战\"现在做进生产、跑 14 天三遍\"的建议 | 核实属实的：资本开支那一行在新句子下 12 次读漏 3 次（旧句子 9/9，模型两次都怪\"更大的行\"半句）；句子照 5 月财报改、又只在 5 月财报上量，没有留出的财报；做进生产前的记录写法（同一个数挂几道题、指引不该写成\"事实\"、第二个提示词）要 Alex 定；分类和判断同时跑、说明里还引着旧句子，照实记下 | 建议撤回；下一步：修掉资本开支漏读（改成\"写完逐条复核\"），在 5 月和留出的 8 月两份财报上各测一遍，约 0.5 美元 |\n| 36 | 11-05 | Alex：\"好开始做到production 上，完整的更新所有系统设计等\"；同一个数挂几道题，他选\"存一条，挂到每道读到它的题\"（D364）。做进生产前先修资本开支漏读：第四版把\"是不是这道题的量\"挪到最后逐条复核（并删掉别的期间），文件规则补\"有申报的只读申报的\"；Codex 审 3 轮（共 6 条严重，都改）；试发 7 道题过；然后 5 月登记读法、8 月留出读法 | **没过**：5 月\"不能删掉该留的\"——v22 只留住 1/3、资本开支 3/6 读；8 月资本开支二季度 0/3（选了上半年、引用跳格被拒）。机理：复核里\"别的期间删掉\"让全年题删掉最近一季；\"最近一期\"在本季和年初至今两栏间没说清。好消息：8 月 v9 找到了新披露的担保 1,085 亿和承诺 560 亿 | 停，交 Alex：第三版是唯一过了 5 月三条的版本 |\n| 37 | 11-05 | Alex：\"为什么没过？…你确定是正确的rejection 吗？你又下去看trace吗？\"；\"我需要你深度看完所有失败trace给我准信下一步你要跑什么才能收敛\"。普查全部 7 次读法、606 次文件读（`census_all_reads.py`，$0） | 第三版 0 个错数、156 次读漏 3 次（全是资本开支）；第二版 2 个错数；第四版漏 24 次（5 月）、16 次（8 月）。我自己判错的：6 个对的数被我的引用检查拒（漏星号、跳格），8 月\"只认本季\"规则错，第 13 轮 3 条\"有争议\"的数是标准答案自己用的行，第三版全过后又改第四版 | 收敛方案：提示词定为第三版不再改；修引用检查（$0 重放全部 606 次读核对）；在 8 月财报上用第三版读一次（约 8 美分，只有\"收错数\"能叫停）；然后做进生产 |\n| 38 | 11-05 | Alex：\"好，按这三步做，你不要再搬石头砸自己脚了，你要收敛上生产\"。第 1 步：引用检查搬进正式代码 `src/hivemind/baseline.py`，加\"行名是报告的、数在同一行就存原文那一整行\"的修复（漏脚注记号、跳格）；对照 36 例全对，三个弄坏的版本各抓出 1 个错；重放全部存下的读法，改变的正好是那 6 个被拒的对数。第 2 步：第三版加修好的检查读 8 月留出财报 132 次（0.096 美元），两人分类 | 第 1 步：只改了那 6 条。第 2 步过：44 个数 0 个错（3 条\"剩余资本开支承诺 70 亿\"两人不一致，对着原文定为\"自己的量，别的期间\"）；v10 3/3、v12 2/3 | 读法定为第三版加修好的检查，不再改；第 3 步写正式代码 |\n| 39 | 11-05 | 第 3 步：做进正式系统（设计四张表，Codex 审 3 轮：第 1 轮 4 条严重、第 2 轮 2 条严重，都改；第 3 轮无严重问题） | 建成 `baseline.run` + poc-v116 + baseline-v3 提示词文件；$0 核对：44 份请求和验证时逐字节相同，3 次存下的回答走正式代码写出的记录完全一样，第一天判断正好判这些题，网页从开始跟踪那天可见；新测试 12 条、6 个弄坏版本都抓出、全套 272 条通过；设计页和 PRD 00/03/04/05/06 更新，`docs/check.py` 通过 | 交 Alex：要不要跑 14 天三遍完整验收（约 5 美元） |\n| 40 | 11-05 | Alex：\"跑验收\"。14 天三遍完整验收：poc-v116（开始跟踪时读财报）三遍、当天重跑 poc-v108 三遍作对照，冻结尺子打分（事先锁定 `acceptance-design.md`）；电脑中途在电池上睡了约 5 小时，6 遍被暂停，插电后自己接着跑完 | **全过**：v10、v12 各 3/3（对照从没判过）；合计 53 对 45（满分 57，+8）；唯一少两次的 v17（0/3 对 2/3）两人都认定不是起点数：同一份抽取请求，新配置两遍碰巧留下\"中国份额归零\"那句，对照没留；约 4.79 美元 | 交 Alex：poc-v116 是否成为默认 |\n| 41 | 11-05 | Alex：\"都做\"（poc-v116 设成默认；提交代码、开 PR）。默认配置改成 poc-v116，默认的条目数据库换成带财报网页原文的那一份（旧的没有原文，新默认会在它上面拒跑）；测试按用户的用法补上：不给种子题就拒绝，给了就先读财报再跑第一天 | 测试全过，5 个弄坏的版本都抓出；配置的设置和验收三遍记下的校验码一致（只改了配置里的注释）；花钱前的检查脚本在新配置的运行数据上照常跑完，但不复查读财报那一步的引用检查（记为未补的缺口）；D366 | 提交、开 PR；下一类问题等 Alex |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && cat codex-r56.md codex-r56b.md codex-r56c.md'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && cat codex-r56.md codex-r56b.md codex-r56c.md'","aggregated_output":"**STOP on one confirmed line. Reject the blanket `%` and `x` cutoff.** The saved answer used $108B to derive a growth rate and $112.5B as its Q3 revenue. The proposed fix also accepts an answer that uses $108B as the dollar starting point for Q4 while counting $112.5B for Q3.\n\n1. **Serious — The verdict is right under the adjudication procedure used in both runs.** Both refusal reviewers judged the P-v4 answer right. I reconciled all 12 first replies with the saved requests and checker results. All 12 passed the schema, 11 published, and one was refused. There are 24 first readings and 12 adjudication readings across six packets. Every case has at least one usable reply, and both joint replies have both forecasts supported. The Part A logs show 104 passing cases, 40 caught mutants plus the control, and 19 passing rehearsal checks. I independently reran the 104 cases against both checker versions. [Registered lines](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:244) · [Refusal](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind2-2026-11-22/CHECKED.json:138) · [Refusal review](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind2-2026-11-22/refusal-review/P-v4-claude.codex.json:3) · [Part A logs](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/small-cases.log:105) · [Mutants](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/small-mutants.log:42) · [Rehearsal](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/small-rehearsal.log:20)\n\n   **Wording — R07 has two disputed defects on F3.** One reader flagged an estimate presented as the market’s reference. The other flagged two values for the same quantity. The registered line requires agreement on the named defect itself. Each adjudicator pair split, so neither defect adds a confirmed stop under the first run’s agreement rule. I would write “one confirmed stop, with unresolved marks” because the registration says a third reader settles disputes, and the procedure used here added two adjudicators who could still disagree. Across the six packets, five marks were jointly rejected, nine split, and zero were jointly upheld. [R07 votes](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind2-2026-11-22/TALLY.json:157) · [First run’s procedure](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND-RESULT.md:37) · [Registered wording](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:252)\n\n   **Minor — Two details in the write-up need correction.** Only E’s Claude writer copied the two CPU-market figures and exercised the range fix. The write-up also omits R11’s split over F13, which assigns a time period and a funded/unfunded scope to an outside $70B figure. F13 feeds neither the outcome nor the reference. [E source](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind2-2026-11-22/E/user.txt:30) · [E Codex reply](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind2-2026-11-22/E/answers/codex.json:1) · [F13 votes](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind2-2026-11-22/TALLY.json:377)\n\n2. **Serious — The proposed checker change is wider than Alex’s ruling.** I reproduced the reported census: one of 24 saved replies changes, and the candidate passes all 104 existing cases. I then tested a variation of the saved P-v4 reply. It keeps the $112.5B Q3 forecast in the annual sum and projects Q4 by applying the guided growth factor twice from Q2: `96.2 × (108 / 96.2)² = 121.25`. The first multiplication reconstructs the $108B Q3 guidance as the dollar base for the second. The reply passes the schema. The current checker refuses it on S4 alone, and the candidate publishes $411.57B. A second probe also flipped when Q4 company sales were calculated as `$116B ÷ ($99.9B / $108B)`. Neither probe needs to relabel the original Q3 guidance. Alex approved using guidance to set a growth benchmark while the forecast supplies the quarter’s dollar value. The cutoff lets a ratio carry the second dollar value into the outcome. [Alex’s exact question and answer](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11348) · [Saved P-v4 reply](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind2-2026-11-22/P-v4/answers/claude.json:1) · [$99.9B source](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind2-2026-11-22/P-v4/user.txt:613) · [Candidate cutoff](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/s4-ratestop-calc_small.py.txt:638)\n\n3. **Serious — Change both request sentences with the narrower checker fix.** The system asks writers to carry guided growth forward. The schema says the rate can inform an `estimate`, which is a specific figure type, and the header can be read as requiring every calculation path to go through the quarter forecast. A code-only change leaves that tension in place. I would say that a growth rate derived from guidance may inform an estimate or be used in `apply_growth` with the shared quarter’s forecast as the dollar base. The header should require the single forecast wherever the calculation uses that quarter’s **value**. Drop the reflection’s parenthetical that a growth rate is another quantity. The unit alone cannot tell whether the calculation uses it as a benchmark or to recover a second dollar value. Give readers the same distinction. [System text](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/judging-v13s.txt:4) · [Schema wording](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:152) · [Header](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:176) · [Proposed wording](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/claude-r56.md:21)\n\n4. **Serious — Disclose the $18B split as affecting O’s answer. D741 ruling 2 leaves it open.** The sources report a $25B July balance and $18B committed for the rest of the year. They do not establish that the $18B is included in the July balance or will all be paid by year-end. Those assumptions can support a conditional forecast. They do not establish a $7B company-schedule reference just because the subtraction carries no past share. R11 presents the funding schedule as something the company said and states only the overlap as an assumption. Without the deduction, the July balance alone starts in rung 2. The first run split on the same passage. This adds no registered stop and needs no Alex ruling before the $0 checker test. If the council still disagrees when deciding whether to advance, put the reference question to Alex explicitly. [Original passages](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind2-2026-11-22/O/user.txt:36) · [D741 ruling 2](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11356) · [R07 adjudication](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind2-2026-11-22/adjudication/R07.codex.json:9) · [First run’s split](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND-RESULT.md:58)\n\n   **Minor — Wrong numbers confined to prose are a disclosure under this test.** The registered definitions cover copied and computed figures. The errors still matter to a reader. R09’s example reaches $430.82B against a $431.2B threshold, and R11’s full-slip scenario gives $32B on its own assumptions. Neither adds a registered stop or needs Alex before the next $0 test. Making prose accuracy a stop condition would be a separate decision. [Reader definitions](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind_test.py:169) · [R09 arithmetic](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind2-2026-11-22/adjudication/R09.codex.json:20) · [R11 arithmetic](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind2-2026-11-22/adjudication/R11.claude.json:49)\n\n5. **Recommendation and falsifier.** Narrow the checker to the demonstrated use of guidance as a growth benchmark, align the request and reader wording, and replay the 24 saved replies. The repair fails if R03 still refuses, either counterexample publishes, or another saved decision changes. Once that check passes, record the council decision and run **one fresh $0 blind test** with the revised request and the disagreement procedure stated up front. The old replies can prove what the checker does. Fresh replies show how writers read the new wording. Any registered stop keeps the work in council. A clean run goes to Alex with both disclosures for the separate paid-run decision. [Council authority](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4871) · [Registered next step](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:267)\n\nNo files were edited. The two counterexamples ran in memory.**Do not build the narrowed change.** It publishes an answer that counts **$112.5B** for Q3 in the annual sum, then resets Q4’s starting amount to the **$108B** Q3 guidance. The current checker refuses that answer.\n\n1. **Serious — The growth-rate exemption still lets a second quarterly value into the outcome.** I changed the saved P-v4 reply to start Q4 at `$112.5B × (1 + growth($112.5B, $108B))`, then grow that starting amount by 12%. The first step gives exactly $108B. The narrowed checker publishes **$411.28B** because it sees the adopted forecast in the base and skips the rate that cancels it. The same probe with the quoted guidance range publishes **$408.86B–$413.70B**. When I put the guidance directly in the base calculation as a dollar deduction, the narrowed checker still refused it. In a separate joint-answer probe, a Q4 Data Center base inherited the $110B company Q3 forecast through Q4, and a rate built from Q3 reset it to the $108B guidance basis. That also published. [Checker diff](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/r56b/calc_small.py.diff:22) · [Arithmetic](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:230) · [Saved P-v4 answer](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind2-2026-11-22/P-v4/answers/claude.json:1) · [Joint fixture](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/small_cases.py:80)\n\n   **Minor — `rests_on` is an existing reader case.** I put the same substitution in a Q4 estimate that explicitly relied on the $108B guidance as its starting amount. Both versions published and recorded the competing Q3 figures. The check for two adopted forecasts follows `rests_on`. The check for bypassing a listed forecast follows arithmetic inputs. D738 assigns the use of a number inside an estimate to readers. [D738](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11258) · [Adopted forecasts](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:594) · [Reader records](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:732)\n\n2. **Serious — The code is both wider and narrower than Alex’s answer.** Alex approved using guidance to inform a 13% Q4 forecast when $113.6B supplies the only Q3 dollar amount. I encoded that example as a 13% estimate resting on the guidance-implied rate. Both versions published. The narrowed code also published when the rate used the outside $113.6B estimate in place of guidance. In the other direction, it refused the saved answer when I wrote the same Q4 calculation as `$112.5B × ($108B / $96.2B)`. The recomputed annual outcome was still **$416.62B**. It also refused the new Data Center example when I expressed the same $101.75B starting amount as an estimate resting on the shared company forecast and the mix. The rulings record puts the meaning of the benchmark in the request and reader brief. [Alex’s exact ruling](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11346) · [Outside estimate](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind2-2026-11-22/P-v4/user.txt:258) · [Checker diff](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/r56b/calc_small.py.diff:22)\n\n3. **Wording — State the dollar-value rule consistently.** The schema says *guidance*, while the code skips any qualifying percentage. The header calls it the “one exception” and says “built on,” which leaves writers guessing whether an estimate resting on the forecast qualifies. Both reader versions preserve the single-dollar-value condition, but mentioning `apply_growth` invites readers to treat the operation as proof. The system’s “run-rate that carries the guided growth forward” leaves all of those readings open. Use the same plain rule across all four places: guidance can set the pace, and the adopted forecast supplies the quarter’s dollar value. Tell readers to look through the rate for a second dollar value. Any restriction on how writers must express the arithmetic belongs in the request. [System text](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/judging-v13s.txt:4) · [Schema and header diff](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/r56b/render_v13.py.diff:10) · [Reader diff](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/r56b/blind_test.py.diff:10) · [Adjudicator diff](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/r56b/blind_adjudicate.py.diff:3)\n\n4. **Minor — Both new mutants are decisive, and one of the three refusal cases overlaps an existing check.** Both new passing cases fail with the exemption disabled. I also tried requiring the forecast as the immediate base. Only the Data Center case failed, so it earns its place. The Q2-built run-rate is the only case that catches removal of the base condition. The repeated-multiple case catches a return to the blanket cutoff. The explicitly labelled rebuilt Q3 still refuses under the current, blanket, narrowed and no-base versions because the walk sees the rebuilt Q3 figure before reaching its rate. It adds a computed-figure example to the existing direct-bypass check. All 109 cases and all 42 mutants reproduced in memory. The stored-reply replay also reproduced one change in 24, the saved P-v4 refusal. The decisive missing pair is the saved valid answer and the guidance-reset version that this round showed can publish beside it. [New cases](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/r56b/small_cases.py.diff:17) · [Existing bypass case](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/small_cases.py:388) · [New mutants](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/r56b/small_mutants.py.diff:10) · [Stored-reply census](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/s4_census.py:1)\n\n**Verdict — Do not build.****Choose A′ with revised wording.** The saved answer used $112.5B for Q3 and used guidance to set Q4’s pace. The blanket change would also let an answer quietly switch Q4’s starting point back to $108B.\n\n1. **Serious — Keep S4.** D738 explicitly checks whether the arithmetic reaches a figure for a listed shared quantity without going through its forecast. D741 approves using guidance to inform an estimate. Alex’s example uses the roughly 12% guided pace to choose a 13% Q4 forecast, then applies 13% to the one Q3 forecast. The saved reply instead feeds the historical guidance-derived rate straight into the Q4 calculation. Its $416.62B result is financially defensible, as both refusal reviewers found. The way it was written still triggers the existing check. I replayed two guidance-reset examples in memory. The current check refused both, and B published both. The “one quantity, several figures” note also appears when guidance legitimately supports an estimate, so it cannot tell an analyst which happened. That trade favors A′ under D737 and D738. [D737 and D738](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11236) · [D741](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11346) · [Saved answer](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind2-2026-11-22/P-v4/answers/claude.json:1) · [Refusal review](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind2-2026-11-22/refusal-review/P-v4-claude.codex.json:3) · [Reader note](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:752)\n\n2. **Serious — The proposed wording still misses the boundary.** “Never as an input of a computed figure” bans more than the code does. “For a shared quantity” can also point writers at the wrong quantity. I checked all three cases in memory. [S4 implementation](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:594)\n\n   - **Unlisted quantity.** Removing Q3 from the shared list made the identical arithmetic pass. The separate check for two adopted forecasts still applies to unlisted quantities. [Shared-quantity check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:615)\n   - **Outside Q3 figure.** Replacing guidance with the outside $113.6B produces the same refusal when the rate feeds Q4 directly. It passes when the outside rate informs a stated Q4 growth estimate. Readers still judge whether adopting that pace is supported. D741 specifically approves the guidance example. [Outside figure](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind2-2026-11-22/P-v4/user.txt:258) · [D741](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11348)\n   - **Data Center.** The direct rate is refused when the segment outcome reaches the listed **company** Q3 guidance through that rate. The same arithmetic passes when the writer states and supports an estimated **segment** growth rate using the company rate as a benchmark. The segment’s own Q3 forecast supplies the dollar base. [Joint fixture](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/small_cases.py:58) · [Joint request](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind2-2026-11-22/P/user.txt:8)\n\n   **Wording — Change the header too.** Say “Follow every arithmetic path from each outcome, including through rates and multiples. For each listed shared quantity and period, the first figure of that quantity on every path that reaches it must be the same forecast.” In the system text, ask writers to *use guidance to inform the pace they forecast*. “At the guided pace” reads as requiring the exact rate. In the schema, say to record the chosen future pace as an estimate, explain why it applies, and name the benchmark in `rests_on`. The chosen rate can then feed the dollar calculation. That version passed with the same $416.62B and preserved recomputable arithmetic. Give readers the proposed instruction to look through rates for a second dollar value, including inside stated assumptions. [System instructions](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/judging-v13s.txt:4) · [Schema and header](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:112) · [Reader brief](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind_test.py:169)\n\n3. **Serious — Keep the stop line and register how readers apply it.** Record two judgments independently. Was the forecast and its reasoning financially sound? Did the exact request clearly state the condition that triggered refusal? A sound answer refused under a clear condition still stops the run. Calling it wrong solely because it broke the format would remove the protection the second half of the stop line provides. Registering those two questions up front preserves the bar and the previous STOP. Use the registered third reader to settle disagreements on the specific finding. Give the wording reviewer the system text, user text, and schema. The current adjudication packet omits the system text, which contains the instruction at issue here. [Registered stop and reader procedure](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:244) · [Adjudication packet](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind_adjudicate.py:71) · [Prior STOP](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND2-RESULT.md:3)\n\n4. **Minor — Agree to one fresh $0 run with 12 writers after the wording and the procedure are registered.** First replay the saved refusal and the two reset examples, and show that the stated-estimate version passes. Keep the saved refusal as a test of the stated format, with its financial correctness still open to blind review. A fresh, financially sound refusal sends the format back to council. An accepted answer confirmed to carry two quarterly dollar values sends the publication decision back to council. Only a complete run that meets every registered line, including a usable answer for each case and both supported forecasts in one joint reply, goes to Alex for the paid-run decision. No files were edited. [Registered cases and next step](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:255)\n\n**Verdict — A′ with revised wording and the existing stop line.**","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
