{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cd poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22 && head -10 S/writer-prompt.txt && rg -n 'a rung whose band|market.s reference|F8|F12|F14' reader-packets/R01.md | cut -c1-210 && rg -n 'answers/rung|arithmetic|quote_number' adjudication/R08.md | head -8 | cut -c1-230 && rg -n '\\\"case\\\": \\\"S\\\"|\\\"v6\\\":' CHECKED.json\"","aggregated_output":"You are a writer in a blind test of a forecasting request. In the folder /Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/S there are three files you may read:\n- system.txt: the system message of the request;\n- user.txt: the user message of the request;\n- schema.json: the JSON schema your answer must satisfy (strict structured output: every property present, null where a field does not apply).\nRead those three files and nothing else: no other file in any folder, no web, no tools beyond reading those three files.\nAct as the model that receives this request: do the analysis the system and user messages ask for, and return your answer as one JSON object that satisfies schema.json exactly.\nReturn only the JSON object, with no text before or after it.\n11:               own estimate passed off as the market's reference | broken structure>\", \"figures\": [\"<figure ids>\"], \"detail\": \"...\"}]}\n23:- own estimate passed off as the market's reference: a figure marked as the market's reference is, or rests on, the writer's own\n27:  the question's quantity, or a rung whose band does not hold the outcome. A total used for a narrower quantity (total capital\n283:      \"rests_on\": [\"F4\", \"F5\", \"F1\", \"F2\", \"F3\", \"F8\", \"F9\", \"F10\", \"e4405\"],\n307:      \"id\": \"F8\",\n383:      \"id\": \"F12\",\n416:      \"rests_on\": [\"F11\", \"F12\", \"e4082\", \"e5014\", \"e1649\"],\n421:      \"id\": \"F14\",\n446:      \"reasons\": \"Rung 4 (at least $700bn and below $800bn). Reference: outside tallies of the four companies' own 2026 guidance put their combined capital expenditure at roughly $720-745bn (F8, e5014), whi\n11:- wrong arithmetic: a computed figure does not equal its operation on its inputs.\n30:- Reader 1 marks a defect: wrong arithmetic (figures ['F14', 'F15']): Using the stated inputs, F14 is 111.62 × 93% = 103.8066, which rounds to 103.81, and F15 is 128.36 × 93.5% = 120.0166, which rounds to 120.02. The listed res\n60: \"figures/quote_number\": \"Source only: a complete number exactly as the quote writes it, never a piece of a longer number, range or 'plus or minus' expression, with its currency and scale or its percent sign, and nothing else: \n69: \"answers/rung\": \"Forecast only: the rung whose band holds the outcome as the code recomputes it (a band includes its lower edge, not its upper); for a range outcome, a band it overlaps, with the reason in reasons.\",\n81:Shared quantities, one forecast figure each; on every arithmetic path from an outcome, through rates and multiples too, the first figure of that quantity reached is its forecast: NVIDIA, revenue, company, FY2027 Q3; NVIDIA, rev\n855:      \"evidence_id\": \"e2295\", \"quote_number\": \"$361 billion\", \"qualifier\": \"none\",\n863:      \"evidence_id\": \"e109\", \"quote_number\": \"$75.25 billion\", \"qualifier\": \"none\",\n871:      \"evidence_id\": \"e5079\", \"quote_number\": \"$89.02 billion\", \"qualifier\": \"none\",\n427:  \"case\": \"S\",\n478:   \"v6\": [\n487:  \"case\": \"S\",\n535:   \"v6\": [\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
